Common AWS architecture (recommended)
Frontend (React / Mobile)
        ↓
API Gateway
        ↓
Lambda / Backend
        ↓
DynamoDB (user profile + email)
        ↓
SES (send emails)
        ↓
Cognito (auth & users)

Where emails are stored
| Purpose               | Service         |
| --------------------- | --------------- |
| Login / auth email    | Cognito         |
| User profile email    | DynamoDB / RDS  |
| Sent emails           | SES (logs only) |
| Email content history | S3 (optional)   |
Security best practices:
Never store plain passwords
Encrypt data at rest (default in AWS)
Use IAM roles (not access keys)
Enable SES DKIM + SPF
Enable Cognito MFA if possible

Simple recommendation (short answer)
If you’re on AWS:

Users → Amazon Cognito

Emails (data) → DynamoDB

Send emails → Amazon SES

